{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will set My face, etc.</b> — these are faces of wrath. And the reason the forces of judgment are called ״faces״ is because the company of the destroyers — they are the company of the annihilators — always stand before HaShem; therefore they are called ״the face of HaShem,״ and concerning them He said ״And I will set My face.״ And by this, ״and you shall be smitten before your enemies״ — they are the nations, who are the branches of the forces of the kelippah. Further, the statement <b>My face</b> intends to say that He will not hide His face from them when He delivers them into the hand of their enemies — for if He did, heaven forbid, they would consume the vineyard. And He revealed His blessed will at the end of the matter: ״and yet for all that, etc. I have not rejected them to destroy them״ (Leviticus 26:44). And He said ״in you״ to exclude the Holy Temple — that the attribute of judgment shall not hold sway over it first."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The word כרם ('vineyard') likely refers to Israel metaphorically, as in Isaiah 5."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:01.208073644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}